        {
          "label": "Post 5",
          "text": "In case you missed Cubs news today:\n\n> ⚾ Cubs agreed to terms with Hiromi Itoh\n   - The 29-year-old Nippon Ham righty won the Sawamura Award in 2025 as Japan's best pitcher\n   - 3.18 ERA, 172.2 innings, just 34 walks in 2026 — exceptional command for a starter\n   - Pending physical; terms have not been disclosed\n   - Expected to slot as the No. 4 or No. 5 in the 2027 rotation\n\n> ✅ Trevor Rogers 5yr/$120M is now OFFICIAL\n   - Passed his physical Friday; Bob Nightengale confirmed the deal is complete\n   - Posted a 2.90 ERA with 119 strikeouts over his final 20 starts (121 IP) in 2026\n   - Strongest run of pitching in his career; rejected Baltimore's $23.15M qualifying offer\n\n> 📋 The Cubs' 2027 rotation through today: Rogers · Itoh · Assad · Steele (TJ rehab) · Horton (mid-2027) · Ben Brown (first half)\n\n> ⚠️ CBA expires Tuesday. MLB and MLBPA meet in Phoenix this weekend in a last-ditch push\n   - Owners want a salary cap and floor; union says MLB hasn't added a dollar in pay\n   - Lockout hits at 11:59 PM ET on Tuesday, December 1\n\n> 🔄 Michael King (12-10, 3.26 ERA) is still unsigned — Cubs and Mets remain in the mix\n\nOne of these every night. Follow for the daily Cubs recap.\n\n#Cubs",
